# B0 (no card opened): build the window image tp4-rh-1 from the pushed tp4/round-host commit. The profile named is the production default; nothing is baked as the image default
# (no C2_BAKE_DEFAULT_PROFILE). THE TAG MUST BE FRESH: the build step skips a tag that already exists. round_host.py is the one new served module; the flags are read in verify_prestage.py, packed_verifier.py,
# serving_packed_step.py, serving_packed_bridge.py, serving_worker_hook.py, early_draft.py, dflash_packed_proposal.py, dflash_packed_proposal_coordinator.py and quad_draft_tp.py: all in both image copy lists and the overlay.
# READ: the build log's provenance report with no problem line, the closure checks pass, the image id printed. Never run it during a timing job. Duration (estimate): 20-60 min. Stop rule: a build or provenance failure stops the window.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/round-host window (docs/tp4-round-host.md; scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/round-host and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards
# are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from this branch by its author. ORDER.txt has the order, the classes, the minutes, the NEEDS graph and every read rule.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-rh-1 is what B0 builds from the pushed tp4/round-host commit; every later job serves that one image. A commit of a file the image
# carries needs a new B0 build and a new tag in every template. The cards are under development: this window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=build
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-rh-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4
